{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Astigmatism Correction}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Astigmatism_Correction}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Anchor Properties Dialog}
\b\fs36\cf1 Astigmatism Correction
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx12685\pard\intbl \{bmc bm12.bmp\}  Before you try to correct astigmatism, check whether \uldb \b aperture alignment\plain\b\fs24 {\v 334XEAC@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24  and
\par\intbl \uldb \b Beam Alignment\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1LKD_PL@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24  are correct , because wrong adjustment of these simulates astigmatism.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Use a magnification which is high enough to clearly display astigmatism (generally 10KX), with small, circular or rectangular features in the image.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Use \uldb \b Reduced Raster Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reduced_Raster_Mode}\plain\fs24  for fast image update.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm13.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx12685\pard\intbl 
\par\intbl Through focusing will lead from one privileged focus direction (above) to another (right).
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} With \b FOCUS FINE\plain\fs24  adjust an image quality which lies between the two images.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Call the \uldb \b SEM Control Apertures\plain\b\fs24 {\v 295DOW3@TabMgr.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm14.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx12685\pard\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Use \ul scroll bars\plain\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar} on \b SEM Control Panel\plain\fs24  to compensate astigmatism - one direction at a time 
\par\intbl or
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Use \b Autostig\plain\fs24  on Stigmation Panel if noise in the image is low and features are well defined.
\par\intbl Verify by through-focusing that there are no more privileged directions. Otherwise repeat the procedure.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl For additional information see \uldb \b Stigmation Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stigmation_Mode}\plain\fs24 .\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm15.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
