{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 Cleaning
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The entire LEO Electron Microscope must be kept clean, especially:
\par 
\par \pard\li705\fi-705\tx355 \b \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Worktable surfaces and specimen holders must be clean and dust-free to prevent contamination of specimen and specimen chamber.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab All parts which are in vacuum or brought into it must be handled with care. Use lint free gloves to avoid grease and sweat on the parts. Use forceps to hold small parts and specimen stubs. 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Use only approved solvents for cleaning.
\par 
\par See  \uldb Cleaning Methods-Instrument surfaces\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cleaning_Methods}
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 For all other parts see  \uldb \b Cleaning Recommendations\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cleaning_Recommendations@maint.hlp} \plain\fs24 which is part of\b  \uldb Maintenance\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@maint.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Cleaning Methods-instrument surfaces}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Cleaning_Methods}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Cleaning Methods- Instrument surfaces
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Do not use solvents to clean surfaces. 
\par Moisten soft cloth in soap water and wipe surfaces. Make sure that no humidity penetrates the instrument.
\par 
\par 
\par For all other parts see  \uldb \b Cleaning Recommendations\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cleaning_Recommendations@maint.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
