{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Collector Adjust}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Collector_Adjust}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Collector Adjust
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Call \uldb \b SEM Control panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@TabMgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  with \b <CTRL + G>\plain\fs24   and select the \uldb \b SEM Control Detectors\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1WE3854@TabMgr.HLP}\plain\fs24  tab.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Locate Detectors frame and then the Collector Bias field \{bmc bm34.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\} Use \ul Scroll Bar\plain\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar} to adjust the voltage of the collector from -250 V to +400 V.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Negative Collector Bias\plain\fs24  repels low energy secondary electrons and lets only pass the high energy backscattered electrons traveling on straight lines towards the collector. This results in a spotlight illumination casting long shadows and enhancing topography. The Chamber Secondary Electron Detector is in \b Backscatter Mode.\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Positive Collector Bias\plain\fs24  attracts low energy secondary electrons. This result in homogeneous illumination on the specimen, bright fringes from edge effect, topography is dominant. The Chamber Secondary Electron Detector is in \b Normal Mode.
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Double \ul click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on the Collector Bias field to open the \b Enter New Parameter Value\plain\fs24  window. Enter a value from the keyboard.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab Click on the Collector Bias field with the right mouse button to open the \uldb \b Predefined List\plain\b\fs24 {\v Predefined_List}\plain\fs24  window.
\par 
\par See also \uldb \b Parameter Control Analogue\plain\b\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Analogue}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \page
