{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Depth of Focus}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Depth_of_Focus}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs28 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx4535\cellx5035\cellx8085\pard\intbl Depth of Focus
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 The vertical distance (WD 1, WD 2), over which the sample appears to be in focus (S) depends on the incidence angle and hence on the aperture used. 
\par\intbl A large aperture (red) results in short depth of focus (WD1) and a small aperture (blue) gives a high depth of focus (WD2)\cell\pard \pard\intbl \b\fs28 \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm42.wmf\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
