{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Display Monitor}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Display_Monitor}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Display Monitor
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5665\cellx6445\cellx14035\pard\intbl The Display Monitor displays the desktop of the Windows software and on it the application window of the LEO-32 Scanning Electron Microscope software. From here the instrument is controlled.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The minimum you may have on display after start-up is the \uldb \b Top Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Top_Window}\plain\fs24  (1) within which appears the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24  (3). Other components may be called up as required, either explicitly (e.g. by menu selection) or as a response to some action or event.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \f11 The monitor is 17" SVGA,1024 x 768 resolution, non interlaced, colour. Optional 21" size.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl When the system is started up you will usually also have the \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\f11\fs24  (2) and the \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}\plain\f11\fs24  (4) displayed.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl See also \uldb \b SEM Control\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Contents@tabmgr.hlp}\plain\f11\fs24  and \uldb \b SEM Dialogs\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Contents@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 \cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl \b 1
\par\intbl 2
