\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7365\cellx10985\pard\intbl \{bmc bm17.bmp\}  \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} \b Dyn Focus\plain\fs24  \ul Check box\plain\fs24 {\v Check_box} to switch the function on \{bmc bm4.bmp\}.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Use \ul \b\ul Scroll bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar}\plain\fs24  of \b FCF Angle\plain\fs24  to adjust for tilt. 
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 See \uldb \b Alignment of Dynamic Focus\plain\b\fs24 {\v Alignment_of_Dynamic_Focus}\plain\fs24 .\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm24.bmp\}  Dynamic Focus is effective in \b vertical direction\plain\fs24 , and the inclination of the specimen surface must be adjusted so that  the upper edge of the image is at the specimen position with the longest working distance, and the lower edge at the one with the shortest working distance or vice versa.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl Use \b SCAN ROTATION\plain\fs24  and rotate image until the above condition is fulfilled.\cell\pard \pard\intbl     \{bmc bm50.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par This panel also contains the controls for \uldb \b Scan Rotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Scan_Rotation}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Tilt Correction\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tilt_Correction}\plain\fs24 .
