{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Focus Adjustment}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Focus_Adjustment}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Focus Adjustment
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The focus is correctly adjusted when the image on the screen is sharp and clear. There are two ways to achieve this:
\par \uldb \b Focusing on the specimen\plain\b\fs24 {\v Focusing_on_the_Specimen}\plain\fs24  or \uldb \b moving the specimen with the stage to the focus plane\plain\b\fs24 {\v Moving_the_Specimen_to_the_Focus_Plan}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par The \ul \b\ul Working Distance\plain\b\fs24 {\v Working_Distance}\plain\fs24  is displayed in the \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \uldb \b Automatic focusing\plain\b\fs24 {\v Auto_Focus}\plain\fs24  on the specimen surface is also provided.
\par 
\par For highly tilted specimen surfaces use \uldb \b Dynamic Focus\plain\b\fs24 {\v Dynamic_Focus}\plain\fs24  for optimum results.
\par \pard 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Focus Wobble}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Focus_Wobble}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Focus Wobble
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par Focus Wobble sweeps the focus of the objective lens backwards and forwards through focus on the specimen plane. When the aperture is misaligned a lateral shift is observed.
\par 
\par Focus Wobble is activated  from \uldb \b SEM Control Apertures\plain\b\fs24 {\v 295DOW3@tabmgr.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\tab \b Focus Wobble\plain\fs24  can be directly activated from the \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\fs24  by clicking on  \{bmc bm63.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx12115\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Focus Wobble is active when the panel pops up.\par\pard \pard\intbl\li275\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Adjust strength of wobble with the \b Wobble Amplitude\plain\fs24  \ul scroll bar\plain\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar}.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Select wobble speed with checking \b Wobble Fast\plain\fs24  \{bmc bm4.bmp\} .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Switch Focus Wobble OFF by \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on \b OFF.\plain\fs24  
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl       \{bmc bm64.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par For additional information see \uldb \b Focus Wobble Special Settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v Focus_Wobble_Special_Settings}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Focus Wobble Special Settings}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Focus_Wobble_Special_Settings}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Focus Wobble Special Settings
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par The Look and Feel for Focus Wobble can be configured for each user. To do this
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Select \b User Preferences\plain\fs24  from the \uldb \b Menu Tools\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Tools_User_Preferences}\plain\fs24  or \{bmc bm1.bmp\} type \b <ALT + T>\plain\fs24  and then \b <U>\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par to open the \uldb \b Preference Selection Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v 6T9R6I@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24 .and \ul click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on the \uldb \b SEM Conditions\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1F9HBAX@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24  Tab.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Focusing on the Specimen}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Focusing_on_the_Specimen}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Focusing on the Specimen
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Focus is adjusted by \ul dragging\plain\fs24 {\v Drag} the mouse on the\b  \uldb Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24 .when the \uldb \b Mag/Focus Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mag_Focus_Mode}\plain\fs24  is selected.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm22.bmp\}\tab Drag with the middle mouse button in horizontal direction.
\par 
\par Moving right takes the focal plane to longer \ul working distance\plain\fs24 {\v Working_Distance} and moving left to shorter working distance.
\par 
\par The working distance is displayed in the \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}\plain\fs24  \b :\plain\fs24  \ul M\plain\fs24 iddle \ul B\plain\fs24 utton: WD = xxx mm  \{bmc bm65.bmp\}.
\par 
\par Focus sensitivity is magnification compensated. So, if you must change the focus over long working distance adjust a lower magnification first, focus and then go back to high magnification to fine focusing.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The overall focus sensitivity for the adjustment with the mouse can be changed between \b fine\plain\fs24  and \b coarse\plain\fs24  in the Status Bar:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab  \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on \{bmc bm32.bmp\}   to switch to  \{bmc bm31.bmp\}  and vice versa.
\par 
\par For additional information about parameter setting see \uldb \b Parameter Control Analogue\plain\b\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Analogue}. 
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \page
