{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} small}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm70.bmp\}  Freeze / Unfreeze Icon (Icon 24)
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The standard functions of this Icon are described below but may be changed by the user with the \uldb \b Tool Bar Editor\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar_Editor}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Left \b  \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click}\b  \plain\fs24  on the icon to \b pause\plain\fs24  the scan and \b freeze\plain\fs24  the image. A second click starts the scan again and \b unfreezes\plain\fs24  the image.
\par If in split or quad mode the freeze/unfreeze applies to the currently selected \uldb \b zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v ZONES@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par A frozen zone displays a blue dot in its lower right corner.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 Freeze and Unfreeze can also be performed from \uldb \b Menu Scanning Speeds\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Scanning_Speeds}\plain\fs24  
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm18.bmp\}\tab Middle click is undefined 
\par 
\par In the \uldb \b Preference Selection Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v 6T9R6I@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24  under \uldb \b SEM Conditions\plain\b\fs24 {\v 9TLKMY@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24  a flag can be set so that the beam is blanked when all zones are frozen.
\par 
\par \b Use Edit - Annotate\plain\fs24  in \b Help\plain\fs24  to provide your own help for this icon.
\par User annotation has been added if there is a paper clip icon \{bmc bm19.bmp\} in this help. \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on it to view the help text.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Function Key Macros}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Function_Key_Macros}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Function Key Macros
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab The function keys \b <F5>, <F6>, <F7>, <F8>, <F11>\plain\fs24  and \b <F12>\plain\fs24  (with and without \b <SHIFT>\plain\fs24 ) may be used to execute installed \ul macros\plain\fs24 {\v Macro},
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 e.g. pressing \b <F6>\plain\fs24  causes the installed macro with identifier \b F6\plain\fs24  to be executed.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Similary pressing \b <SHIFT + F6>\plain\fs24  causes the installed macro with identifier \b SHIFT F6\plain\fs24  to be executed.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm24.bmp\}\tab If the macro does not exist a '\b BEEP\plain\fs24 ' is given.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm24.bmp\}\tab If the macro exists but a macro is already running a double 'BEEP' is given.
\par 
\par If no such macro exists the key press will be ignored.
\par 
\par Refer to the Help for \uldb \b Macro Functions\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@leom.hlp}\plain\fs24  for details of macro facilities.
\par \page
