\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Gallery
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The Image Gallery gives an overview over the images stored in the selected directory: 
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx4535\cellx14105\pard\intbl The path is shown in the blue top line of the window. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl See also \uldb \b Gallery Overview\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1PQQZOQ@gallery.hlp} \plain\fs24 for detailed information
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl A \ul Scroll Bar\plain\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar} on the right to the display window allows to scroll through the image gallery.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Click on an image to select it and to display it's properties. The User Text is displayed in the bottom status line .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Double Click on the image to select it for loading and leave the image gallery.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm103.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Leave the image gallery by clicking on \{bmc bm104.bmp\} without any change.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Image Store}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Image_Store}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b Image Store
\par \plain\fs24 The image store holds the 8 bit wide data which may be loaded from the input scan via the input chain. 
\par The  data is loaded into zones according to the operating mode. The noise reduction mode determines how the stored and live data are combined in the store.
\par 
\par 
\par Data may also be loaded/read by program (e.g. Import TIFF and Export TIFF and Clipboard functions).
\par 
\par The contents of the store is passed through the Display LUT to the Display Monitor.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Image Window}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Image_Window}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Window
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par The Image Window is used to display the SEM information either live or stored (frozen). It may occupy the whole screen of the monitor or may be overlaid with other information like the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24 , the \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}\plain\fs24 , the \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\fs24  and other panels like the Annotation Panel etc.
\par The Image Window may be reduced or split in half showing different SEM image information in those zones.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab With \b <SHIFT + F3>\plain\fs24  the bars can be switched OFF or ON. In the OFF state the image covers the full screen. However, panels will stay on.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm105.bmp\}\tab When the mouse cursor is on the image window the mouse may be used to adjust parameters. Parameters can be assigned to the mouse buttons depending on the mode of operation. 
\par 
\par See \uldb \b Image Window Adjustment Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window_Adjustment_Mode}\plain\fs24  for further information.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 TIFF files (*.TIF and *.TIFF) and JPEG files (*.JPG) may be \uldb \b dropped\plain\b\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop}\plain\fs24  onto the Image Window.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Image Window Adjustment Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Image_Window_Adjustment_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Window Adjustment Mode
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par When the mouse cursor  \{bmc bm106.bmp\}  is on the Image Window different \b Adjustment Modes\plain\fs24  are available:
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Parameter Adjustment Mode:
\par \plain\fs24 In this control mode the mouse is used for parameter adjustment. The parameters are shown in the \uldb Status Bar\plain\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}.
\par Coarse and fine can be toggled with \b <TAB> \plain\fs24 or by clicking on the appropriate field in the Status Bar.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab \ul Dragging\plain\fs24 {\v Drag} with the \b left button\plain\fs24  changes the parameter either coarse or fine, depending on the mode setting. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm18.bmp\}\tab Dragging with the \b middle button\plain\fs24  changes the second parameter.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v Click} the \b right button\plain\fs24  opens the \uldb \b Mode Selection Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mode_Selection_Panel}
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs28 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Control Raster Mode:\plain\fs28 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 In this control mode the mouse is used to manipulate the size and position of scan raster objects.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 When the mouse pointer is inside the scan zone the mouse performs as above. If the pointer is near the edge, the icon changes. Now the left button is used to drag and position the frame.
\par \pard\tx355 Clicking on the frame borders allows to seize the frame. For further information see \uldb \b Reduced Raster Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reduced_Raster_Mode}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Import Image Dialog}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Import_Image_Dialog}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Import Image Dialog
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par This dialog box handles the importing (loading) of images saved in TIFF (Tag Image File Format) into the image store. It consists of three tabs, labeled Load, Standard Data and User Data. The top bar (caption) of the box shows the directory being accessed.
\par The dialog box is accessed through 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b File - Load Image\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par or through
\par 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab right mouse button on the Image Window with \b Import TIFF\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par or through
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \b <CTRL + O>\plain\fs24  from the keyboard.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The TIFF files in the current \uldb \b Image Directory\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Directory}\plain\fs24  are displayed in a list box. The image directory path is displayed in the caption and may be changed with a dialog panel in 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Tools - \uldb User Preferences\plain\b\fs24 {\v 6T9R6I@leoserv.hlp} -  Image Directory Setup.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par  For a detailed description see \uldb \b\fs28 Image Import\plain\b\fs28 {\v 1JWFSX0@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
