{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Closing the Interface}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} YDV_M4}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 Closing the Interface
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\f11\fs24 This function is called from the system menu and terminates the operation of the LEO-32 User Interface.
\par \f4 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \f11 In the Menu Bar \ul click\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Click} on \b File\plain\f11\fs24  and \b LOG OFF 
\par \plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx10985\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f11 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab For safety you are requested to confirm the action and to close the \b U\plain\f11\fs24 ser \b I\plain\f11\fs24 nter\b F\plain\f11\fs24 ace.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab <OK>\plain\f11\fs24  starts the close down action.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab <Cancel>\plain\f11\fs24  breaks it off and returns to the application.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl The action is as follows:\cell\pard \pard\intbl     \{bmc bm108.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Save operating\f4  conditions if re\f11 quired.
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Save in files any user specific data in the \uldb \b User Directory\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v 5LDQJ4@leoserv.HLP}\plain\f11\fs24 , and record the current user directory.
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Terminate the Windows LEO UIF application.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The server is still running and may be closed if required by clicking the server application on the Task bar \{bmc bm109.bmp\} 
\par \pard\tx355 and then clicking the application close button \{bmc bm104.bmp\}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 If the LEO icon is double clicked the server and the SEM application is started again.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Instrument Shut-down}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Instrument_Shut_down}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \f4\b\fs36\cf1 Instrument Shut-down
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 This function shuts down Windows and removes the power from the computer, the display monitor and the SEM electronics. The vacuum system stays ON.
\par \pard\li705\fi-705\tx355 
\par \pard\li705\fi-705\tx355 \b \{bmc bm20.bmp\}\tab Before you attempt to shut down the instrument, make sure to follow an orderly exit sequence on the SEM application by following the procedures given in  \uldb Closing the Interface\plain\b\fs24 {\v YDV_M4} and \uldb Server Shutdown\plain\b\fs24 {\v CLOSE@leoserv.hlp}. Otherwise loss of data will be possible.
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \b \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm110.bmp\} in the Desk Top's Task Bar and select <Shutdown>
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Press the Windows \{bmc bm111.bmp\} key and navigate (\uldb Cursor Movement Keys\plain\b\fs24 {\v Cursor_Movement_Keys}) to <Shutdown> and press <ENTER>.
\par \pard\li705\fi-705\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx9895\pard\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab On theComputer Housing locate the  \b Standby Button\plain\fs24  (2), lift the safety flap and press it. \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl The computer is powered down.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \pard\intbl\li705\fi-705 \b          \{bmc bm112.wmf\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li705\fi-705 
