{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Navigation Box}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Navigation_Box}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Navigation Box
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \f11 The Navigation Box provides visual indication of the range and current value of one- and two-dimensional parameters.
\par \f4 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx9895\pard\intbl \f11 The top line shows the operation the box is used for (e.g. Beam Shift)
\par\intbl The edges of the box represent the limits of the variable range (e.g. - 100%, +100%) and cross hairs indicate the CENTER OF THE BOX, not necessarily the center  of the range.
\par\intbl The current parameter value is indicated by a red marker.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm17.bmp\} The parameter value may be adjusted by \ul dragging\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Drag} the marker to the required position.\cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl           \{bmc bm142.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par Alternatively the X and Y values may be individually adjusted using the \ul Scroll Bars\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar} and the parameter(s) set to zero using the origin button (labeled with \b 0 \plain\f11\fs24 at the junction of the Scroll Bars.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Noise Reduction Principle}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Noise_Reduction_Principle}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \f4\b\fs36\cf1 Noise Reduction Principle
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The signal entering the image processor is made up of two components, image and noise. Image is the signal of interest and correlates with the object being scanned, noise is random in nature.
\par 
\par Therefore by averaging multiple scans of the same area, the signal will be reinforced, while the noise will be reduced. This is the basis on which the noise reduction works.
\par 
\par See 
\par \uldb \b Scan Rate and Noise Reduction\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1BUL_CS@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \uldb \b Using the digital store\plain\b\fs24 {\v 6YWPDO@operation.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \pard \uldb \b Noise Reduction\plain\b\fs24 {\v 2ME28UE@tabmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
