{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Parameter Control Analogue}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Parameter_Control_Analogue}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Parameter Control Analogue
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \f11 The User Interface controls the SEM by interface components which include:
\par 
\par \b Analogue Parameters\plain\f11\fs24  (usually referred to as \b Parameters\plain\f11\fs24 ).
\par 
\par These are values such as accelerating voltage and are expressed in appropriate units e.g. EHT = 30 kV 
\par 
\par Adjustment methods  (not all methods are available on all parameters) are:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b Mouse adjustment\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window_Adjustment_Mode}\plain\f11\fs24  in \uldb \b Image Window\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\f11\fs24  of selected parameter(s)
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b Navigation Box\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Navigation_Box}\plain\f11\fs24  control of the selected parameter
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \ul \b\ul Scroll Bar\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar}\plain\f11\fs24  either dedicated or selected to the parameter.
\par \f4 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx11555\pard\intbl \f11 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}  \b Keyboard Entry \plain\f11\fs24 (double \ul click\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Click} left or middle button on displayed value) to open an input panel.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Type value as required (magnification of 554 in this example).\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 Preset value selection is from a \ul \b\ul Drop-down List\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Drop_down_List} \plain\f11\fs24 or from \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 a\b  \uldb Predefined List\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Predefined_List}.\par\pard \pard\intbl \plain\f11\fs24 \cell\pard \pard\intbl           \{bmc bm145.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Parameter Control Digital}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Parameter_Control_Digital}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \f4\b\fs36\cf1 Parameter Control Digital
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \f11 Digital Parameters (usually referred to as \b States\plain\f11\fs24  ) are variables which represent specific states of control such as Focus Wobble and may only have a restricted set of values such as ON and OFF. e.g. Focus Wobble = OFF.
\par \f4 
\par \f11 States may change as a result of events within the SEM or requests by the user 
\par 
\par \f4 \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab \f11 If a state is displayed then selecting it with the Left Mouse button will have the following effect: (unless read only or disabled)
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b Toggle:\plain\f11\fs24  The state is changed to the other value. A \ul checkbox\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Check_box}  \{bmc bm4.bmp\}  usually indicates the state.
\par 
\par \b Selection:\plain\f11\fs24  The list of currently permitted states or \ul radio buttons\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Radio_Button}  \{bmc bm137.bmp\}  on control panels are displayed for user's choice
\par 
\par States may also alter as a result of changes in the SEM internal state (e.g. completion of a function).
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Commands\plain\f11\fs24  are initiated either by selecting a state change or by panel buttons.
\par \page
