{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Predefined List}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Predefined_List}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Predefined List
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab \f11 If the right mouse button is pressed over a displayed analogue parameter value (provided it is read/write and enabled) the \b Predefined List\plain\f11\fs24  is displayed with the list of already defined values.\f4 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx13815\pard\intbl \f11 Below the list box is a text entry window, characters typed here will be matched to the entries in the list box and the nearest match highlighted.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Selecting a list box entry will cause the parameter to be set to the label value.
\par\intbl To indicate if the parameter is currently set to the highlighted entry the legend \b actioned!\plain\f11\fs24  will be displayed when this is the case.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Buttons are provided for ADD, DELETE, UNDO, HELP and CLOSE.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm147.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx13815\pard\intbl \b ADD\plain\f11\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li275 This function brings up a name entry dialog box into which the user may type any string of text to identify the current parameter value. The current parameter value is  not shown but is taken from the value which is current when the user enters the predefined list. 
\par\intbl \b OK\plain\f11\fs24  will enter the position and label into the list.
\par\intbl \b CANCEL\plain\f11\fs24  will remove the data entry box without action.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li275 \pard\intbl        \{bmc bm148.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard \b DELETE \plain\f11\fs24 
\par \pard\li275 This function deletes the currently highlighted list box entry from the list.\b 
\par \pard UNDO \plain\f11\fs24 
\par \pard\li275 This function causes the parameter to be set to the value which was current when the dialog box was selected.\b 
\par \pard HELP\plain\f11\fs24  
\par \pard\li275 Opens this help topic.
\par \pard \b CLOSE \plain\f11\fs24 
\par \pard\li275 This function closes the Predefined List dialog box. All list entries for the parameter are saved in the \uldb \b User Directory\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v User_Directory}\plain\f11\fs24  as a file whose name is derived from the parameter mnemonic and the extension \b PRE\plain\f11\fs24  (e.g.\b  Brightness.PRE\plain\f11\fs24 ).
\par \page
