{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Printing Images}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Printing_Images}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Printing Images
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Whether you can take a micrograph or a videoprint will depend on the configuration of the microscope, i.e. what hardware has been installed on the microscope. Also standard printers become more and more competitive since their performance has been increased remarkably. Printing can be performed in two ways:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \b All parameters have been set and printing of the images is a routine job:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Use \b  Print Image\plain\fs24  from \uldb \b Menu File Print Image\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_File_Print_Image} 
\par or 
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Use the shortcut \b <CTRL + P> 
\par or
\par \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Click on the\uldb \b  Printer icon\plain\b\fs24 {\v Printer_icon}\plain\fs24  \{bmc bm149.bmp\} with the left mouse button \{bmc bm17.bmp\}.
\par \b 
\par \{bmc bm20.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 The printing will not function if you have not done at least one print from the \b Print Setup\plain\fs24  dialog to establish the printing settings.\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \b Set or check SEM parameters for printing:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Use the \uldb Print Setup Dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v DVXXAS@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  from \uldb \b Menu File Print Setup\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_File_Print_Setup} 
\par or
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab  \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} with the right mouse button on the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24  and call \b Send to\plain\fs24  and \b Printer\plain\fs24  with the \uldb \b Mode Selection Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mode_Selection_Panel}.
\par or
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\tab Click on the Printer icon \{bmc bm149.bmp\} with the middle mouse button \{bmc bm18.bmp\}.\b 
\par \page
