{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 SEM Status
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \f11 The SEM Status panel can be accessed by \b <CTRL + I>\plain\f11\fs24  or from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\f11\fs24  from \uldb \b View, SEM Status\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v Menu_View_SEM_Status}\plain\f11\fs24 .\f4 
\par \pard\tx355 \f11 
\par \pard\tx355 The SEM Status Panel shows 3 tabs for\b  Display\plain\f11\fs24 ,\b  Select\plain\f11\fs24  and \b File\plain\f11\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx12115\pard\intbl \ul \ul Clicking\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Click} on \b Display\plain\f11\fs24  brings this tab forward and displays a user selected group of parameters which are continuously updated.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The parameters also provide a means of adjustment by click and double click. See \uldb Analogue\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Analogue} and \uldb Digital\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Digital} adjustment
\par\intbl Clicking on a Command executes it.
\par\intbl \b 
\par\intbl \plain\f11\fs24 When the system is shutdown the current status display contents is saved in the \uldb \b User Directory\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v 18YPI2P@leoserv.HLP}\plain\f11\fs24  as file \b Current.STS\plain\f11\fs24 . Also the display contents can be saved, loaded, or cleared using the procedures given in the \uldb \b SEM Status File\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Status_File}\plain\f11\fs24  tab.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl When the system is started up the status display contents are restored from the current user directory.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Multiple parameters may be selected for display from the
\par\intbl \uldb \b SEM Status Select\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Status_Select}\plain\f11\fs24  tab.\cell\pard \pard\intbl           \{bmc bm136.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm104.bmp\} to close the window.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} SEM Status File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} SEM_Status_File}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \f4\b\fs36\cf1 SEM Status File
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab \ul \f11\ul Clicking\plain\f11\fs24 {\v Click} on \b File\plain\f11\fs24  brings this tab forward and displays the three commands which are available from here.
\par \f4 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx12115\pard\intbl \f11\b Load\plain\f11\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li275 This function invokes the standard file load dialog which displays the \b St\plain\f11\fs24 atus \b Selection\plain\f11\fs24  files (extension \b .STS\plain\f11\fs24 ) in the current \uldb \b User Directory\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v 18YPI2P@leoserv.HLP}.\par\pard \pard\intbl \plain\f11\fs24 If a file is selected it's contents replaces the current selection in the SEM Status Display.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b File Save\plain\f11\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li275 This function saves the current contents of the \uldb \b SEM Status Display\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Status}\plain\f11\fs24  to a user defined filename (extension .STS, status selection). By default the file is saved in the current User Directory.
\par\intbl \b \par\pard \pard\intbl Clear Display\plain\f11\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li275 This function clears the current selection from the SEM Status Display and resets the \uldb \b SEM Status Select\plain\f11\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Status_Select}\plain\f11\fs24  list as well.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li275 \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl            \{bmc bm155.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm104.bmp\} to close the window.
\par \pard\tx355 
