\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Call \b Scan Rotation\plain\fs24  through calling the Rotate / Tilt panel:
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Call \b Scanning\plain\fs24  with \b <ALT + S>\plain\fs24  and \b <T>\plain\fs24  for the \b Rotate / Tilt\plain\fs24  panel.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7365\cellx10705\cellx13795\pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} \b Scan Rot\plain\fs24  \ul Check box\plain\fs24 {\v Check_box} to switch the function on \{bmc bm4.bmp\}.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Use \ul \b\ul Scroll bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Scroll_Bar}\plain\fs24  to set the Scan Rotation Angle. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm24.bmp\}\tab \b Mechanical rotation by the specimen stage
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 \tab The stage is rotatable mechanically through 360\'b0 relatively to the scan field. A specimen can be observed under different angles especially when tilted, because the axis of rotation tilts with the specimen. The specimen rotates relatively to the detector so that it is always "illuminated" from the same direction, e.g. from the upper right.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm24.bmp\}\tab \b Electrical rotation by Scan Rotation\plain\fs24  
