{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Split Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Split_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 Split Mode
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab The function is selected from \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24  with \b\ul S\plain\b\fs24 canning\plain\fs24  and the item \b Sp\plain\b\fs24 lit
\par or\plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\tab On the \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\fs24  click on \uldb \b Split Mode Icon\plain\b\fs24 {\v Split_Mode_Icon}\plain\fs24  \{bmc bm151.bmp\}  
\par 
\par \b  or\plain\fs24  from the Mode Selection Panel.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab The \uldb \b Mode Selection Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mode_Selection_Panel}\plain\fs24  is activated when the right mouse button is pressed while the mouse cursor is on the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par This mode scans a zone on the specimen twice in succession and then displays the two zones on the left and right half of the Image Window.
\par \pard\tx355 The centers of the two zones are equal to the scan center on the specimen in Normal mode.
\par 
\par Associated with each zone is a set of parameters determining the acquisition of the parameters.
\par Different detectors can be assigned to each zone and each zone can be frozen independently of the other.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab An anchor icon identifies the active zone (icon is green) and can be \ul dragged\plain\fs24 {\v Drag} to either of the zones thereby switching the active zone.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab By double \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v Click} the anchor icon is changed (shanks are red) which indicates that both zones are controlled in parallel.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab Clicking on the icon with the right mouse button opens the \uldb \b Anchor Properties Dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v Anchor_Properties_Dialog}.
\par 
\par \page
