{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Backlash}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Backlash}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs28 Stage Backlash
\par \plain\f11\fs24 Backlash is the term used to describe the 'slack'  between the mechanical components of the stage which may cause positional inaccuracies according to the direction of approach to a position. To overcome this a technique called 'backlash correction' is used to ensure that a point is always approached from the same direction. \f4 
\par \page
