\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Status Bar
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par The Status Bar is shown at the bottom of the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window} \plain\fs24 if it is enabled.
\par 
\par The Status Bar is switched on by:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b View Tool Bars\plain\fs24  with \b <ALT + V>\plain\fs24  and then \b <T>\plain\fs24  from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar} 
\par \plain\fs24 \tab The \uldb \b Tool Bar Views\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_View_Tool_Bars}\plain\fs24  menu pops up and then select the Status Bar with \b <S>\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Type \b <CTRL + B> \plain\fs24 to access the \b Tool Bar Views\plain\fs24  pop up menu and then select the Status Bar with \b <S>\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab Click with the right mouse button on the Tool Bar if it is activated. Select Status checkbox \{bmc bm4.bmp\}.
\par 
\par The left side of the Status Bar shows either results or hints e.g. \{bmc bm198.bmp\} .
\par 
\par If a dynamic process is under way a \ul progress bar\plain\fs24 {\v Progress_Bar} is displayed:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm150.bmp\} (in this example running up of the gun is shown).
\par 
\par The right side of the Status Bar displays parameters which are controlled by the mouse when it is in the Image Window and provides status/control of the Vacuum system and Gun.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm199.bmp\}
\par 
\par See \uldb \b Status Bar Parameter Control\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar_Parameter_Control}.
\par \plain\fs24 
