{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Store / Restore System Conditions}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Store___Restore_System_Conditions}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Store / Restore System Conditions
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 One of the most useful features of a software controlled microscope is the ability to save  the operating conditions of the microscope in a file that can be used at a future date to set up those exact conditions again. For the LEO-32  series, the microscope conditions are stored as a \ul macro\plain\fs24 {\v Macro}. It is set up automatically when you save conditions. Recalling microscope conditions executes the contents of the macro file. 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Store:
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx12115\pard\intbl\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm24.bmp\} \tab When the microscope is shut down, the conditions may be saved to disk. The file saved is always called RESTOREx.MLC (x is detemined by the filament type), thus the latest RESTORE file will always over-write the previous one. 
\par\intbl The file is saved in the current user's directory, so that each user can also have his own set of microscope condition files: \b ..\'5cUSER\'5cGUEST\'5cRESTORE0.MLC\plain\fs24  with MLC standing for 
\par\intbl \b M\plain\fs24 acro\b  L\plain\fs24 ibrary \b C\plain\fs24 onditions and the 0 for a Tungsten filament.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \b\fs28 \par\pard \pard\intbl           \{bmc bm210.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 Restore:
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v Click} on \b File\plain\fs24  in the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Vacuum_Specimen_Change}\plain\fs24 , then select \b Restore\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Type \b <ALT + F>\plain\fs24  then \b <R>\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\tab On the Tool Bar click the\b  Restore \plain\fs24 icon \{bmc bm153.bmp\}.
\par 
\par The latest RESTORE0.MLC file from the user's directory is loaded and the macro SYSTEMS CONDITIONS is executed setting the systems parameters to the previous state. If the file is not found the \uldb \b Standard\plain\b\fs24 {\v Z1JVVC@leom.hlp}\plain\fs24  function is executed
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
