\pard\keepn\tx355 \fs36\cf1 User Directory
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 A User Directory contains all the user specific files, e.g. \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\fs24 , macro library, macro files, machine conditions, status list etc. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 On \b User LogOn\plain\b\fs24 {\v LogOn}\plain\fs24  the Current User Directory is set as defined in the User Profile held in the Administrator Database.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm219.bmp\}\tab It is recommended that each user has his own individual User Directory.
\par 
\par 
\par The \uldb \b Administrator\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@admin32.hlp}\plain\fs24  may grant a User the right to change and select any User Directory. See \uldb \b User Directory Setup\plain\b\fs24 {\v 5LDQJ4@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Where a user does not have \b User Directory Change Privilege\plain\fs24  a directory higher than the directory defined by the Administrator may not be selected, although sub directories may be created and selected. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The User Directory on LogOn is set to the User Directory which was current on \ul LogOff\plain\fs24 {\v LogOff}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Software conventions}
