{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Software Conventions
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The LEO Electron Microscopes are completely computer controlled and software driven. The LEO-32 Series software is a normal Windows application running under Windows95 and therefore obeys all the usual rules of Windows applications. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} WI6FA8}
\b\fs28 Windows Operating System
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 If you are familiar with Windows you already know the essential terms and operations and are ready to learn how to use the Scanning Electron Microscope.
\par \pard\tx355 It you are unfamiliar with Windows you should read at least Chapters 1 and 2 of the Windows User's Guide which is supplied with your system.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1_.C8DP}
\b\fs28 SEM Software
\par \pard\tx355 
