\par \pard\tx2265\tx5095\tx6805 \b\fs28 \{bmc bm105.bmp\} The {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} MOUSE}
Mouse
\par \pard\tx2265\tx5095\tx6805 \plain\fs24 The mouse is the primary adjustment and selection control of the microscope. There are carefully defined conventions governing its use:
\par \pard\tx2265\tx5095\tx6805 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm17.bmp\} \tab \b The left button:\plain\fs24 
\par The normal Windows convention of pointing and clicking is used for icon selection or menu selection, dragging is used for moving or sizing objects and for parameter adjustment.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm18.bmp\}\tab \b The middle button:\plain\fs24 
\par The middle button is used for parameter adjustment.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm107.bmp\}\tab \b The right button:
\par \plain\fs24 The right mouse button is used to display a pop-up menu while over the image.
\par When the cursor is over an icon and the right button is pressed, the control panel associated with that icon will pop up.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab The {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 2P.VEL}
Keyboard
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 In addition to the mouse control of parameters, many keyboard keys have been assigned to special functions acting as "accelerators" or "short cut keys" and giving direct access to the function. For a list of short cut keys see \uldb \b Keyboard Keys\plain\b\fs24 {\v Keyboard_Keys}.
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs28 \{bmc bm221.bmp\}\tab \b The {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 18KV.W7}
Monitor\plain\fs28 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 The monitor serves as the visible link to the user. On its display the SEM image together with all other necessary information for the operation is shown.
\par \pard\tx355 Appearance can be selected by switching \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Bar}\plain\fs24 , \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Bar}\plain\fs24  and\b  \uldb Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24  ON or OFF.
\par \pard\tx355 The resolution of the monitor should be set to 1024 by 768 pixels.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See also\b  \uldb Parameter Control Analogue\plain\b\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Analogue}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Parameter Control Digital\plain\b\fs24 {\v Parameter_Control_Digital}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
