{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} X-Ray Line Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} X_Ray_Line_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 X-Ray Line Mode
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab The function is selected from \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24  with \b\ul S\plain\b\fs24 canning\plain\fs24  and the item \b\ul X\plain\b\fs24 -Ray Line Scan\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 In X-Ray Line Scan Mode a single horizontal line is scanned on the specimen.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The speed is automatically reduced to a maximum pixel average rate of 1024. The parameter \b Line Time\plain\fs24  displays the time to acquire a line of data. Data from multiple lines are collected in a single line time.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm226.bmp\}\tab The line position is indicated by a green raster line which may be \ul dragged\plain\fs24 {\v Drag} using the mouse.
\par 
\par On entering X-Ray line scan mode the data acquisition is initiated. The data from up to 7energy windows (set in the \uldb \b X-Ray setup window\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4NYC_IG@TabMgr.HLP}\plain\fs24 ) is simultaneously loaded into an internal buffer. Data from successive line scans are accumulated.
\par 
\par Each Energy window is identified by a user defined identifier which is defined in the X-Ray setup window.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The line scan data is displayed in a \uldb \b profile window\plain\b\fs24 {\v 41WX_UD@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  in the same manner as the other line profiles (e.g. line scan).
\par 
\par 
