{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Image Capture mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Image_Capture_mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Capture mode
\par \pard \plain\fs24 In normal operation the Image Window is painted with a transparent colour so that the Image in the Image store shows through on the display Monitor.
\par 
\par Under these circumstances if\b  Print Screen \plain\fs24 is used the resulting bitmap does not therefore contain the image because the image is not part of the Windows PC Display. Similarly if remote access is used (e.g. NetMeeting) the SEM image is not available.
\par 
\par In\b  Image Capture mode\plain\fs24  the Image is read from the Image store and pasted into the Image Window, hence the above restrictions do not apply. The image however is not a live image, since this is now hidden behind the bitmap pasted into the image window. A\b  Red Triangle \{bmc bm230.bmp\}\plain\fs24  is displayed in the bottom right corner of the Image Window whenever the image is obscured by a Bitmap.
\par \pard 
\par Image capture mode is switched on/off using the menu \b Tools\plain\fs24  -\uldb \b  Image Capture\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Tools_Image_Capture_Mode}
\par \plain\fs24 A Single Image capture may be performed using the menu \b Tools\plain\fs24  - \uldb \b Capture Now\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Tools_Capture_Now}\plain\fs24 
\par Where remote access is to be used the image capture may be set up to repeat at a specified frequency using menu \b Tools\plain\fs24  -\uldb \b  Image Capture Frequency\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Tools_Image_Capture_Frequency}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
