{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Drag and Drop}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Drag_and_Drop}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Drag and Drop
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Drag and Drop is the technique of transferring files using the Mouse.
\par The File is selected in one Window (Left Mouse button down), dragged to another Window (which may belong to another application) and dropped onto it (release left mouse button).
\par 
\par Example: Files may be dragged from the Windows Explorer and dropped onto a Word Document.
\par 
\par Leo-32 supports the following Drag And Drop functions.
\par 
\par The\uldb \b  Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24  will accept *.TIF, *.TIFF and *.BMP files dropped onto it. This will freeze the image and load the file into the image store. Note: If Leo-32 is executing on a PC in emulation mode the file will become the new backdrop image.
\par \pard 
\par The\uldb \b  Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Window}\plain\fs24  will also accept *.ANN (annotation files) and *.DZ (datazones) dropped onto it. This will load the annotation/datazone.
\par 
\par The \uldb \b Second Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4AHWGBN@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24  and associated Zoom Window will both accept the following files dropped onto them : *.BMP, *.DCX, *.JPG, *.PCX, *.TIF, *.TIFF and  *.XIF
\par 
\par *.TIF Files may be dragged from the\uldb \b  Image Gallery\plain\b\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop@gallery.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
